2. Explain monolithic architecture, service oriented architecture and Micro service architecture.
Monolithic architecture: one code base, all components are packaged as one unit. tightly coupling.
Service oriented architecture: each service performs a specific business functions
Micro service: each service has a single responsibility, services are loosely coupling, services communicate
with each other through api or messaging tools

3. Document the microservice architecture and core components
Docker: container to package services, so services are isolated
Service registry: detect service, so it can be found by other services
Api gateway: all requests come to api gateway, and assign it to corresponding services to handle it
Load balancer: assign requests to available server evenly, avoiding hotspot
Circuit breaker: if a service down, won't affect other services, have a back up plan to bypass the failure service
Kafka: for messaging, handle communication between services

4. Explain Resilience patterns? Explain circuit breaker with Spring Cloud Hystrix code example.
If a service goes down, that request returns an exception or time out, then the connection cut off to prevent
cascading failure. In the mean time provides a back up plan. If a call fail, retry after some time.

5. Explain load balancing algorithms.
a. round robin: connect one by one, like a circle
b. weighted round robin: higher weight gets more request
c. least connection
d. IP hash: hash ip address
e. random

6. Explain API Gateway.
Api gateway is mainly for routing, all requests go to api gateway and it assigns requests to corresponding services
to handle them. It can also serve other functions, like security for authentication and authorization, load balancer

7. Explain service discovery and service registry
Service discovery: a service finds ip of other services
Service registry: like Eureka, a database of service instances. A service will first register itself, registry
periodically check the if the service is healthy

